<title>GERMANY: Thyssen to exit long products business.</title>
<headline>Thyssen to exit long products business.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>German steel group Thyssen AG said on Tuesday it was giving up its long products business as part of an earlier announced shift in strategy.</p>
<p>In a mandatory bourse statement, Thyssen said U.K.-based ISPAT-International would take over Thyssen's Stahl Ruhrort GmbH and Walzdraht Hochfeld GmbH.</p>
<p>Thyssen also said this deal, which was agreed to in principle but still needs regulatory approval, could impact Thyssen shares.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
